# macOS / SMB share artifacts
# The NAS is mounted over SMB, which renames deleted files to .smbdelete*
# instead of removing them. They're invisible in Finder but git will happily
# commit ~28MB of them if you let it.
.smbdelete*
._*
.DS_Store
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.TemporaryItems
.fseventsd

# Local working files — not part of the site.
#
# The deploy rule has always been "nothing starting with _ goes on the server",
# but this listed the underscore files by hand, so every new one had to be
# remembered. It is a wildcard now. The two below don't start with _ and so
# still need naming: CNAME.txt is a stray twin of the real CNAME (no extension,
# and it MUST keep shipping), and CHANGELOG_RUNNING.md is a scratch log.
_*
CHANGELOG_RUNNING.md
CNAME.txt
SITEhandoff.md
node_modules/

# Editor and assistant settings for this machine, not for the site. Left
# untracked these show up in `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all`,
# which is the check "nothing stray can ride along" depends on being empty.
.claude/

# Staging-only files that don't start with _ and so aren't caught above.
# Design mockups get iterated in the open folder before one is chosen, and
# timestamped .bak copies are made before risky edits. Neither belongs on the
# server. `Mocks/` currently holds only _-prefixed files, so it is already
# empty as far as git is concerned — named here so it stays that way.
mockup-*.html
*.bak
*.bak.*
/Mocks/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PUBLIC IMAGE DIRECTORIES — WHITELIST, NOT BLACKLIST
#
# Original camera media now lives under `_review_later/`, but new source folders
# may appear during future work. Ignore every image subdirectory by default and
# re-admit only the nine web-ready directories the public site uses.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
images/*/
!images/brass/
!images/brass-bts/
!images/cracked/
!images/itsaboy/
!images/kit/
!images/lejuice/
!images/lookout/
!images/moz/
!images/scattered/
!images/thehook/
!images/traildead/
!images/og/

# Camera formats, wherever they land. 26 HEIC originals (66 MB) were found
# sitting inside images/itsaboy/ — a whitelisted folder, so the rules above
# would have waved them straight through. Only Safari renders HEIC; Chrome
# and Firefox show a broken image. Convert to JPEG, then ship the JPEG.
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.mov
*.MOV
*.dng
*.DNG
*.arw
*.ARW
*.braw
*.BRAW
